WEBVTT

00:01.170 --> 00:06.170
Are you afraid of opening
your eyes again?

00:06.260 --> 00:11.340
Do you hate being like
a stranger to yourself?

00:21.900 --> 00:24.230
Even if you realize you have no talent

00:24.320 --> 00:26.740
Does that become a pretext
to keep running away?

00:26.820 --> 00:29.070
To respond to the screams
echoing within

00:29.150 --> 00:31.240
Who is there to answer them?

00:31.320 --> 00:35.540
At least, in the few moments
of your life

00:36.240 --> 00:40.250
I want you to be an honest actor

00:40.920 --> 00:43.500
What if today is that day?

00:44.290 --> 00:49.010
Are you afraid of opening
your eyes again?

00:49.090 --> 00:53.430
Do you hate being like
a stranger to yourself?

00:53.510 --> 00:57.270
But you've realized, haven't you?
Your body can't stop moving

00:57.350 --> 01:04.360
"If I think of you, who I can't bear to lose,
my fears seem trivial."

01:06.230 --> 01:09.990
Even if I expose my life and sing

01:11.650 --> 01:15.780
In time, you will understand

01:16.620 --> 01:20.210
Will it end here?

01:20.290 --> 01:23.210
You wouldn't want that, would you?

01:23.290 --> 01:26.540
(Episode 11: The True Name of Cowardice)

01:34.390 --> 01:36.600
The one-thousandth rule.

01:37.220 --> 01:41.020
A conversion formula the Tower uses
for the credit system.

01:41.100 --> 01:47.440
One credit assigned to a monster is equal to
a mage with a strength of 1,000 credits.

01:48.230 --> 01:50.400
A monster worth 270 credits.

01:50.490 --> 01:53.860
Therefore, when converting
a 270-credit monster,

01:53.950 --> 01:55.950
it's equal to a mage with strength of…

01:56.490 --> 01:58.080
…270,000 credits.

01:59.950 --> 02:02.330
Evil Grand Duke!

02:05.420 --> 02:06.540
Dodge it!

02:17.890 --> 02:21.020
You've got to be kidding me!
It's so strong!

02:21.100 --> 02:23.980
Lihanna, we have to retreat!
There's a passageway there.

02:25.060 --> 02:26.150
Run!

02:29.770 --> 02:31.110
Go on ahead!

02:31.190 --> 02:32.190
Hear my call!

02:32.280 --> 02:33.740
Come forth! Grow!

02:33.820 --> 02:35.740
Alfs Ringhul!

02:39.240 --> 02:40.870
Wignall! Hurry up!

02:40.950 --> 02:41.790
Yeah.

02:46.580 --> 02:49.420
It tore my illusion magic
with brute force?

03:06.270 --> 03:08.190
That was way too absurd.

03:08.270 --> 03:10.400
What the heck is that monster?

03:12.190 --> 03:14.820
I've read about it
in the Academy's library.

03:15.360 --> 03:17.320
Evil Grand Duke.

03:17.410 --> 03:21.120
It's a greater-class demon-type of
the evil family on the 25th floor.

03:21.200 --> 03:22.490
The 25th floor?!

03:22.580 --> 03:25.410
What's a monster like that doing here?

03:25.500 --> 03:29.040
It's probably the work of
those mages who used Gate.

03:36.840 --> 03:38.470
Did we outrun it?

03:38.550 --> 03:41.930
No, it's looking for us.

03:42.010 --> 03:44.930
There are so many
Evil Guards and Sentinels.

03:45.020 --> 03:48.940
Grand Duke must have ordered them
to search for us.

03:49.520 --> 03:55.570
So the reason why there's a mass outbreak of
Sentinels on the 11th floor is that monster.

03:58.820 --> 04:01.990
Hey! Are you saying that
we can't escape from here?

04:02.080 --> 04:05.120
We can't get out from this
demon-infested floor?

04:05.200 --> 04:08.250
Are you saying that
we're all going to die here?

04:09.000 --> 04:13.880
We're exhausted, injured,
and in the worst kind of situation…

04:13.960 --> 04:17.880
The despair is crushing
everyone's hearts.

04:17.970 --> 04:20.010
What should we do?

04:20.090 --> 04:21.090
Let's fight.

04:22.600 --> 04:24.970
We've no choice but to defeat
that Grand Duke.

04:27.390 --> 04:29.480
When there's a Baron
or higher-ranked Lord,

04:29.560 --> 04:33.860
Evil-type monsters will establish
a domain across the other floors.

04:34.690 --> 04:39.110
But if we take out the Lord,
they'll lose their chain of command.

04:39.200 --> 04:41.490
It could give us an opening.

04:41.570 --> 04:45.120
Now that the monsters' leader has
been summoned here using Gate,

04:45.200 --> 04:47.200
if we make the lower-ranking
monsters into disarray,

04:47.290 --> 04:49.410
it would make it easier for
the Academy to rescue us.

04:49.500 --> 04:50.750
Is that what you mean?

04:52.540 --> 04:53.670
Don't be stupid!

04:53.750 --> 04:55.710
Have you lost your mind, no-talent?

04:55.800 --> 04:59.380
There's no way we could kill
that monster.

05:00.090 --> 05:01.260
I have a plan.

05:01.840 --> 05:03.510
I can't force it on you all.

05:04.390 --> 05:06.140
Because I can't use magic.

05:06.220 --> 05:07.640
Obviously!

05:07.720 --> 05:09.180
- Who's going to believe in your plan?

05:09.270 --> 05:10.270
- I believe him.
- Who's going to believe in your plan?

05:11.890 --> 05:16.070
I've already been saved several times
by his wisdom and dedication.

05:16.150 --> 05:18.070
I'm willing to trust him too this time.

05:18.150 --> 05:19.900
I believe in him too.

05:19.990 --> 05:22.610
Will knows the dungeon
better than anyone else.

05:22.700 --> 05:27.790
If we're just gonna be chased,
I'd rather stand and fight.

05:27.870 --> 05:31.370
Don't take this as me agreeing
with that flunkee, got it?

05:31.460 --> 05:35.840
Wignall, Colette, and even Sion.

05:35.920 --> 05:40.340
Lihanna, I let him touch me.

05:40.420 --> 05:43.680
I want you to trust an elf's sworn friend.

05:47.010 --> 05:49.680
It seems I've been wrong from the start.

05:50.220 --> 05:54.150
You're not a shield, but a leader.

05:54.230 --> 05:59.690
You're the only one here
who's yet to be crushed by despair.

06:00.440 --> 06:01.780
Lihanna…

06:02.780 --> 06:06.030
If Wignall, whom I trust the most,
believes in you,

06:06.120 --> 06:08.620
then I'll entrust it all to you.

06:08.700 --> 06:10.950
Serfort… No.

06:11.790 --> 06:14.420
Will. Give us the orders.

06:14.500 --> 06:17.250
We'll do as you say.

06:18.210 --> 06:21.630
Got it!
Let's get out of here alive!

06:22.470 --> 06:24.590
Have you all lost your minds?

06:24.680 --> 06:26.760
There's no way we can win
with this no-talent's plan-

06:26.840 --> 06:28.140
You're right, Julius.

06:28.850 --> 06:31.520
My plan alone can't defeat it.

06:31.600 --> 06:32.850
You're the key here.

06:34.020 --> 06:35.900
Please, lend us your power.

06:35.980 --> 06:37.690
What?

06:37.770 --> 06:41.280
I'll teach you the trick of Elfie's spell.

07:01.300 --> 07:02.590
Cage of frozen Earth,

07:02.670 --> 07:04.130
hail that rends the skies.

07:04.220 --> 07:05.050
Far into-

07:06.300 --> 07:07.840
Far into eternity.

07:07.930 --> 07:09.600
The fleeting moments pass.

07:09.680 --> 07:13.100
A lyre of tears,
playing an azure ice melody.

07:13.180 --> 07:15.890
All things fall motionless.

07:16.730 --> 07:19.110
Albis Vina's trick, you say?

07:19.190 --> 07:20.020
Yeah.

07:20.110 --> 07:24.490
Elfie's Ars Weiss allows you
to carry on incantations.

07:24.570 --> 07:25.700
Carry on?

07:25.780 --> 07:29.280
Normally, a spell can't be cast
if the incantation is interrupted.

07:29.370 --> 07:32.370
But with Elfie's Ars Weiss,

07:32.450 --> 07:35.750
you can continue where
the chant stopped.

07:35.830 --> 07:38.620
If a clone gets destroyed and
the incantation is interrupted,

07:38.710 --> 07:41.250
another clone can pick up
the incantation.

07:41.340 --> 07:45.800
By doing that, you can cast advanced spells
that require long incantations.

07:45.880 --> 07:48.680
Offer up the blood,
swear on my corpse.

07:48.760 --> 07:52.510
You think spell-casting is easy?
Damn you, no-talent!

07:52.600 --> 07:57.190
Do they understand
how hard it is to use Ars Weiss?

07:57.270 --> 07:59.730
I can't believe he's making me do this.

07:59.810 --> 08:00.810
Damn it!

08:02.060 --> 08:03.690
I am the protector.

08:05.320 --> 08:07.860
The guard of Narcia's grave.

08:10.410 --> 08:12.030
Everyone, cover Julius!

08:12.120 --> 08:15.290
It's fine to use low-tier spells,
just pin the enemy down!

08:15.370 --> 08:16.290
Colette!

08:16.370 --> 08:17.290
Sion!

08:17.370 --> 08:18.290
Wignall!

08:18.370 --> 08:20.210
- Verdes Lana! - Frubas Julier!
- Ignis Rooks!

08:28.630 --> 08:29.470
It's completely unscathed?

08:29.550 --> 08:30.380
Darn!

08:30.470 --> 08:31.930
It has iron curtain wings.

08:32.010 --> 08:33.760
Just like Will said.

08:44.320 --> 08:48.190
If the information in the library is correct,
the Grand Duke has iron curtain wings.

08:48.280 --> 08:51.530
Which means our attacks
won't get through.

08:52.780 --> 08:54.580
We just need to be decoys.

08:54.660 --> 08:58.660
Until Julius begins his barrage,
we'll divert its attention.

08:58.750 --> 08:59.750
O wind!

09:03.750 --> 09:05.750
Take shape, O coffin of azure steel!

09:07.000 --> 09:09.380
Go forth, O flourishing arctic grove!

09:09.470 --> 09:11.510
Armenta Auliscas!

09:31.530 --> 09:35.700
Julius' trump card,
the ice magic barrage…

09:35.780 --> 09:37.410
It managed to block that.

09:37.990 --> 09:41.210
But it is a monster worth 270 credits.

09:41.290 --> 09:44.630
It might be able to defend
against Julius' trump card.

09:44.710 --> 09:46.090
So, to finish it…

09:46.670 --> 09:47.630
Lihanna!

09:47.710 --> 09:50.460
Owen Sique, Lisolde Dua.

09:52.170 --> 09:53.180
Algiz!

09:53.720 --> 09:56.100
Even if it is able to defend
against the barrage,

09:56.180 --> 09:58.850
the freezing will slow its wings down.

09:58.930 --> 10:01.060
With Lihanna's fast mobility,

10:01.140 --> 10:04.350
she'll be able to maneuver through
and hit where it hurts.

10:07.520 --> 10:10.480
A barrier?
Is it a remote circle?

10:10.570 --> 10:13.150
An automatically activated
barrier on this monster?

10:13.240 --> 10:16.320
Did those mages cast it in advance?

10:17.490 --> 10:18.490
Lihanna!

10:22.830 --> 10:23.660
Kiki!

11:02.410 --> 11:04.790
How could a Grand Duke be there?

11:04.870 --> 11:07.120
Now is not the time to think!

11:07.210 --> 11:08.880
We have to hurry, Workner!

11:09.540 --> 11:10.500
Will.

11:14.380 --> 11:15.260
Mellvent!

11:17.760 --> 11:19.100
Will!

11:21.100 --> 11:22.140
Lihanna!

11:22.220 --> 11:23.930
Are you two okay?

11:24.020 --> 11:26.390
I'm fine.

11:26.480 --> 11:29.400
But Will shielded me.

11:29.480 --> 11:30.310
Will!

11:30.400 --> 11:32.110
Will! Will!

11:37.150 --> 11:39.280
It crushed my ice through brute force.

11:39.370 --> 11:41.660
It's going to attack us!

11:41.740 --> 11:43.290
You have to retreat.

11:43.370 --> 11:45.700
All of you, take Will and run.

11:45.790 --> 11:48.040
I'll buy you some time to escape.

11:48.920 --> 11:52.460
I'll stop that
even if it costs me my life.

11:52.550 --> 11:54.590
What are you saying, Lihanna?

11:54.670 --> 11:59.390
I'm the one who failed to kill it,
so I must do it.

11:59.470 --> 12:02.100
No! You can't!

12:02.180 --> 12:05.560
Do you know why members of
House Owenzaus often die young?

12:06.140 --> 12:10.440
Because as knights,
we have to protect our comrades.

12:12.730 --> 12:14.020
I'll join you.

12:14.110 --> 12:16.400
Wignall? But why?

12:17.030 --> 12:23.080
Lihanna, I've found another Rhizanth
that I respect, like you.

12:29.210 --> 12:31.880
Lihanna! Wignall!

12:31.960 --> 12:34.130
So what do we do now?

12:59.570 --> 13:01.530
Our only option is to run.

13:01.610 --> 13:04.830
Wignall and Lihanna are going to die.

13:05.740 --> 13:08.700
So that their deaths won't be in vain,

13:08.790 --> 13:11.330
the rest of us need to escape from here.

13:11.420 --> 13:13.130
This is not a shame.

13:13.210 --> 13:16.300
There's nothing shameful about this.

13:16.840 --> 13:21.010
To abandon those two and escape…

13:21.090 --> 13:22.300
Sion…

13:23.800 --> 13:26.600
Please… Punch me.

13:31.190 --> 13:33.440
I can't stop shaking.

13:34.610 --> 13:37.820
The goggles Elfie gave me broke.

13:38.820 --> 13:41.070
I'm useless without them.

13:42.030 --> 13:44.200
Without this goggles, I'm…

13:45.030 --> 13:47.620
I'm so scared.

13:49.750 --> 13:51.290
Stop messing with me!

13:51.370 --> 13:53.500
You're the one who lit the fire on us!

13:53.580 --> 13:57.750
It's because you showed us hope!

13:59.760 --> 14:02.680
Lihanna and Wignall are gonna die!

14:02.760 --> 14:06.050
And now you're saying that
you're scared?!

14:06.140 --> 14:08.760
Take responsibility!

14:08.850 --> 14:14.650
Take responsibility for taking us here!

14:14.730 --> 14:18.230
Because of you, that I…

14:18.320 --> 14:20.480
- That we all…
- Sion, stop!

14:28.490 --> 14:31.000
Thank you, Sion.

14:32.040 --> 14:34.460
I stopped shaking.

14:45.510 --> 14:48.010
Colette, take care of Kiki.

14:52.350 --> 14:54.180
What's with him?

14:54.270 --> 14:56.560
He's not scared at all.

14:57.190 --> 14:58.810
He is scared.

14:58.900 --> 15:03.650
Will always has been afraid, even now.

15:03.740 --> 15:06.030
What are you talking about?

15:06.110 --> 15:07.660
Like I'd believe that…

15:07.740 --> 15:09.620
Have you ever held a sword?

15:10.870 --> 15:12.200
What?

15:12.290 --> 15:14.750
Holding wands,
you can cast spells from afar.

15:14.830 --> 15:17.670
But swords can't.

15:17.750 --> 15:22.760
You need to get close to opponents
that are bigger and stronger than you.

15:22.840 --> 15:27.970
Have you ever imagined just
how terrifying that is?

15:28.970 --> 15:30.890
Will is a coward.

15:30.970 --> 15:34.520
No matter how terrified he is,
no matter how pathetic he looks,

15:34.600 --> 15:38.940
he's simply a coward
who's scared of running away.

15:39.020 --> 15:43.030
And that's what people call courage.

15:47.320 --> 15:48.660
I'm going to fight, too.

15:55.080 --> 15:56.540
To hell with that.

15:57.670 --> 15:59.170
You must be kidding.

16:02.920 --> 16:04.760
The enemy's defense is ironclad.

16:04.840 --> 16:10.720
It's so fast for its size,
our attacks can barely hit it.

16:10.800 --> 16:13.510
Thanks to those wings.

16:13.600 --> 16:15.470
In order to defeat the Grand Duke,

16:15.560 --> 16:18.190
we have to sever the wings and
bring it down to the ground.

16:20.100 --> 16:21.610
Pebble Shot!

16:21.690 --> 16:23.110
Colette!

16:23.190 --> 16:25.530
Lihanna and Wignall can't fight anymore.

16:25.610 --> 16:28.070
Colette and I have to do what we can.

16:38.710 --> 16:39.710
So scary.

16:39.790 --> 16:41.880
I don't have my goggles.

16:41.960 --> 16:44.000
I'm scared to death.

16:44.840 --> 16:50.760
But I'm much more afraid of
losing someone.

16:50.840 --> 16:51.890
Colette!

17:01.900 --> 17:04.150
I don't have Kiki with me.

17:04.230 --> 17:08.440
A direct hit will kill me instantly.

17:08.530 --> 17:12.740
But I've seen this attack before.

17:20.910 --> 17:21.750
Will…

17:22.670 --> 17:23.500
That's…

17:25.000 --> 17:27.550
Roar, O cliffs of steel!

17:27.630 --> 17:30.840
Shatter, O stone blade of the chasm!

17:30.920 --> 17:34.010
I'll give Will everything I've got!

17:38.060 --> 17:40.270
Loire Sique!

17:40.350 --> 17:41.730
Golterre!

18:01.960 --> 18:05.460
O embers, last remnants
of the dead city.

18:05.540 --> 18:06.590
Sion?!

18:06.670 --> 18:10.960
Recall it! The memory of flames
that torment thee.

18:11.050 --> 18:12.470
Remember it!

18:12.550 --> 18:15.470
The flames of the scorched Earth
that extinguished thee.

18:15.550 --> 18:21.100
Now, take the burning grief for
a bygone home to burn my foe!

18:21.980 --> 18:23.140
Sion!

18:25.730 --> 18:28.320
He's charging in using
his guardian as a shield.

18:28.400 --> 18:30.360
If you can do it,

18:30.440 --> 18:34.150
There's no way I can't do it!

18:34.240 --> 18:37.830
Iflamme Burdelyon!

18:51.590 --> 18:52.590
Sion!

18:54.930 --> 18:58.350
No way.
Even that didn't finish it off?

18:58.430 --> 19:01.560
It took an advanced spell
at close range, and yet…

19:01.640 --> 19:03.430
What a monster.

19:03.520 --> 19:06.850
A wand can't win.

19:06.940 --> 19:09.900
A sword also can't defeat it.

19:15.110 --> 19:16.610
This is…

19:22.870 --> 19:25.500
Remember, Will.

19:25.580 --> 19:28.130
It's wand and sword.

19:38.930 --> 19:40.550
Are you sure about this?

19:40.640 --> 19:42.100
Stop asking the same question.

19:42.180 --> 19:44.310
I've made my choice.

19:44.390 --> 19:47.900
This is all to protect this world.

19:49.730 --> 19:55.650
One day, wand and sword
will come together.

20:01.700 --> 20:04.490
Wand and sword.

20:08.750 --> 20:10.290
Sion!

20:10.380 --> 20:11.290
I need your spell!

20:11.380 --> 20:12.840
The answer is wand and sword!

20:18.010 --> 20:20.090
Ignis Rooks!

20:28.770 --> 20:30.100
Is that…

20:30.190 --> 20:31.020
No way.

20:34.780 --> 20:35.860
Wis!

20:37.110 --> 20:38.780
What is that?

20:38.860 --> 20:41.280
The sword is clad in flames?

20:41.370 --> 20:44.530
Is it an enchantment?
No, it's different.

20:44.620 --> 20:47.040
The spell was devoured?

20:47.620 --> 20:50.210
Flunkee, you…

20:58.470 --> 21:00.800
Everything I see is red.

21:00.880 --> 21:02.720
I'm brimming with power.

21:02.800 --> 21:06.470
As if urged on by a power
rushing through me.

21:06.560 --> 21:09.310
I found myself muttering the spell.

21:10.520 --> 21:12.350
Fully charged.

21:29.870 --> 21:32.000
Ignis Wis!

23:37.080 --> 23:42.000
Next up, Episode 12 of
Wistoria: Wand and Sword,

23:42.090 --> 23:43.840
"Wand and Sword."
